ecdaa-signature-context: TPM2_SignDigest and TPM2_SignSequenceStart take the ECDAA commit counter from context

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 2 (version 185), "TPMU_SIGNATURE_CTX"):

  "commitCount[sizeof(UINT16)] | BYTE | TPM_ALG_ECDAA | the counter value that
  is used between TPM2_Commit() and the sign operation"

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 3 (version 185), "TPM2_SignSequenceStart",
"General Description"):

  "If the scheme of keyHandle uses a counter value (e.g., TPM_ALG_ECDAA), then
  context shall contain the counter value from TPM2_Commit() to use for the
  signature."

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 2 (version 185), "TPM2B_SIGNATURE_CTX"):

  "context[size]{:sizeof(TPMU_SIGNATURE_CTX)}"

Without ML-DSA, the reference unmarshals a TPM2B_SIGNATURE_CTX with the limit
MAX_SIG_CTX_SIZE = 0 ("185TODO: Incorporate DAA context size"), although its
TPMU_SIGNATURE_CTX has the 2-octet commitCount of ECDAA, so any non-empty
context is TPM_RC_SIZE. The limit is now 2 with ECDAA (and still
MLDSA_CTX_MAX_SIZE with ML-DSA). Also, TPM2_SignDigest and
TPM2_SignSequenceStart select the key's scheme with a NULL selector, which fails for a split signing scheme, and accept no context for
any key other than ML-DSA, so a key whose scheme is TPM_ALG_ECDAA always fails
(TPM_RC_VALUE for its counter in context, TPM_RC_SCHEME without one). For such
a key, context must now be exactly the 2-octet (big-endian) counter
(otherwise TPM_RC_VALUE + RC_<command>_context), and the scheme is the key's
scheme with that counter (CryptoCommon_SelectSignScheme(); failure is
TPM_RC_VALUE + RC_<command>_context). TPM2_SignDigest signs with it, and a
signing sequence keeps it for TPM2_SignSequenceComplete, which consumes the
commit. The other keys are unchanged. As in tpm-rs.
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/include/tpm_public/TpmAlgorithmDefines.h b/TPMCmd/tpm/include/tpm_public/TpmAlgorithmDefines.h
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/include/tpm_public/TpmAlgorithmDefines.h
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/include/tpm_public/TpmAlgorithmDefines.h
@@ -233,8 +233,13 @@
 #endif
 
 // 185TODO: Incorporate DAA context size into the calculation of MAX_SIG_CTX_SIZE.
+// tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+// a TPM2B_SIGNATURE_CTX holds up to sizeof(TPMU_SIGNATURE_CTX) octets (Part 2),
+// which is sizeof(UINT16) (commitCount) for ECDAA without ML-DSA.
 #if ALG_MLDSA
 #  define MAX_SIG_CTX_SIZE MLDSA_CTX_MAX_SIZE
+#elif ALG_ECDAA
+#  define MAX_SIG_CTX_SIZE 2
 #else
 #  define MAX_SIG_CTX_SIZE 0
 #endif
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/SignDigest.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/SignDigest.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/SignDigest.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/SignDigest.c
@@ -85,18 +85,44 @@ TPM2_SignDigest(SignDigest_In*  in,  // IN: input parameter list
     }
 #  endif  // ALG_MLDSA
 
-    // No other key type has a use for a signing context.
-    if(in->context.t.size != 0)
+#  if ALG_ECDAA
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // the commit counter of a key whose scheme is TPM_ALG_ECDAA is 'context'
+    // (Part 2, TPMU_SIGNATURE_CTX: "commitCount[sizeof(UINT16)] | BYTE |
+    // TPM_ALG_ECDAA | the counter value that is used between TPM2_Commit() and
+    // the sign operation"; Part 3, TPM2_SignSequenceStart: "If the scheme of
+    // keyHandle uses a counter value (e.g., TPM_ALG_ECDAA), then context shall
+    // contain the counter value from TPM2_Commit() to use for the signature.").
+    if(signObject->publicArea.type == TPM_ALG_ECC
+       && signObject->publicArea.parameters.eccDetail.scheme.scheme
+              == TPM_ALG_ECDAA)
     {
-        return TPM_RCS_VALUE + RC_SignDigest_context;
+        if(in->context.t.size != sizeof(UINT16))
+            return TPM_RCS_VALUE + RC_SignDigest_context;
+        objectScheme.scheme = TPM_ALG_ECDAA;
+        objectScheme.details.ecdaa.hashAlg =
+            signObject->publicArea.parameters.eccDetail.scheme.details.ecdaa.hashAlg;
+        objectScheme.details.ecdaa.count =
+            BYTE_ARRAY_TO_UINT16(in->context.t.context);
+        if(!CryptoCommon_SelectSignScheme(signObject, &objectScheme))
+            return TPM_RCS_VALUE + RC_SignDigest_context;
     }
-
-    // The signature scheme is dictated by the signObject. Specify a NULL selector
-    // so it gets picked up from signObject and validated.
-    objectScheme.scheme = TPM_ALG_NULL;
-    if(!CryptoCommon_SelectSignScheme(signObject, &objectScheme))
+    else
+#  endif  // ALG_ECDAA
     {
-        return TPM_RCS_SCHEME + RC_SignDigest_keyHandle;
+        // No other key type has a use for a signing context.
+        if(in->context.t.size != 0)
+        {
+            return TPM_RCS_VALUE + RC_SignDigest_context;
+        }
+
+        // The signature scheme is dictated by the signObject. Specify a NULL
+        // selector so it gets picked up from signObject and validated.
+        objectScheme.scheme = TPM_ALG_NULL;
+        if(!CryptoCommon_SelectSignScheme(signObject, &objectScheme))
+        {
+            return TPM_RCS_SCHEME + RC_SignDigest_keyHandle;
+        }
     }
     hashAlg = CryptoCommon_GetSignSchemeHashAlg(&objectScheme);
 
diff --git a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/SignSequenceStart.c b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/SignSequenceStart.c
--- a/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/SignSequenceStart.c
+++ b/TPMCmd/tpm/src/command/Signature/SignSequenceStart.c
@@ -116,6 +116,33 @@ TPM2_SignSequenceStart(SignSequenceStart_In*  in,  // IN: input parameter list
     if(IS_ATTRIBUTE(signObject->publicArea.objectAttributes, TPMA_OBJECT, x509sign))
         return TPM_RCS_ATTRIBUTES + RC_SignSequenceStart_keyHandle;
 
+#  if ALG_ECDAA
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- C-ref spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // the commit counter of a key whose scheme is TPM_ALG_ECDAA is 'context'
+    // (Part 2, TPMU_SIGNATURE_CTX: "commitCount[sizeof(UINT16)] | BYTE |
+    // TPM_ALG_ECDAA | the counter value that is used between TPM2_Commit() and
+    // the sign operation"; Part 3, TPM2_SignSequenceStart: "If the scheme of
+    // keyHandle uses a counter value (e.g., TPM_ALG_ECDAA), then context shall
+    // contain the counter value from TPM2_Commit() to use for the signature.").
+    // The sequence keeps the scheme with the counter, and
+    // TPM2_SignSequenceComplete() signs with it.
+    if(signObject->publicArea.type == TPM_ALG_ECC
+       && signObject->publicArea.parameters.eccDetail.scheme.scheme
+              == TPM_ALG_ECDAA)
+    {
+        if(in->context.t.size != sizeof(UINT16))
+            return TPM_RCS_VALUE + RC_SignSequenceStart_context;
+        scheme.scheme = TPM_ALG_ECDAA;
+        scheme.details.ecdaa.hashAlg =
+            signObject->publicArea.parameters.eccDetail.scheme.details.ecdaa.hashAlg;
+        scheme.details.ecdaa.count = BYTE_ARRAY_TO_UINT16(in->context.t.context);
+        if(!CryptoCommon_SelectSignScheme(signObject, &scheme))
+            return TPM_RCS_VALUE + RC_SignSequenceStart_context;
+        return ObjectCreateSignSequence(
+            signObject, &scheme, &in->auth, &in->context, &out->sequenceHandle);
+    }
+#  endif  // ALG_ECDAA
+
     // Fix the scheme of the sequence to the scheme of the key.
     if(!SelectSignSequenceScheme(signObject, &scheme))
         return TPM_RCS_SCHEME + RC_SignSequenceStart_keyHandle;
